blocks:
  - type: metin
    baslik: What is exam anxiety?
    metin: |-
      Exam anxiety is a state of intense fear and worry that arises in assessment situations. A moderate amount of anxiety can actually improve performance (the Yerkes-Dodson law); but when it becomes excessive, it significantly reduces both study efficiency and exam performance.

      Approximately 25–40% of [university students](/en/blog/university-students-north-cyprus-psychological-support.html) experience clinically significant exam anxiety. Among [international students](/en/blog/mental-health-international-students-famagusta.html), this figure can be higher due to language and cultural differences.
  - type: ozel
    html: |-
      <div class="bg-primary/5 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-primary/15">
                  <p class="text-sm text-ink font-medium mb-2">Symptoms of exam anxiety</p>
                  <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3 mt-3">
                    <ul class="text-xs text-ink-muted space-y-1.5">
                      <li>• Panic before or during the exam</li>
                      <li>• Feeling your mind goes blank</li>
                      <li>• Difficulty concentrating</li>
                      <li>• Procrastination</li>
                    </ul>
                    <ul class="text-xs text-ink-muted space-y-1.5">
                      <li>• Stomach aches, headaches</li>
                      <li>• Sleep difficulties</li>
                      <li>• Heart palpitations</li>
                      <li>• Feeling inadequate</li>
                    </ul>
